      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the first six prime numbers.\n2. Calculate the sum of the first five prime numbers.\n3. Find the sixth prime number.\n4. Compute the remainder when this sum is divided by the sixth prime number.\n\n### Step 1: Identify the first six prime numbers\nThe first six prime numbers are: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, and 13.\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the sum of the first five prime numbers\nThe first five prime numbers are 2, 3, 5, 7, and 11. Their sum is:\n\\[ 2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11 = 28 \\]\n\n### Step 3: Find the sixth prime number\nThe sixth prime number is 13.\n\n### Step 4: Compute the remainder when the sum is divided by the sixth prime number\nWe need to find the remainder when 28 is divided by 13. We do this by performing the division:\n\\[ 28 \\div 13 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\nThis can be verified by:\n\\[ 28 = 13 \\times 2 + 2 \\]\nSo, the remainder is 2.\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
