      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime, let's first list the first six prime numbers.\n\nThe first six prime numbers are:\n\\[ 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the sum of the first five primes:\n\\[ 2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11 \\]\n\nLet's add these numbers step by step:\n\\[\n2 + 3 = 5\n\\]\n\\[\n5 + 5 = 10\n\\]\n\\[\n10 + 7 = 17\n\\]\n\\[\n17 + 11 = 28\n\\]\n\nSo, the sum of the first five primes is:\n\\[ 28 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 28 is divided by the sixth prime, which is 13.\n\nWe perform the division:\n\\[\n28 \\div 13\n\\]\n\nTo find the quotient and the remainder, we calculate:\n\\[\n28 = 13 \\times 2 + 2\n\\]\n\nHere, the quotient is 2 and the remainder is 2. Therefore, the remainder when 28 is divided by 13 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
